urns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Under **Rule 6c-11(d)**, an ETF must keep the following records.\n\n**1. Authorized participant agreements**\n- All written agreements, or copies, between an AP and the ETF or one of its service providers that allow the AP to place creation or redemption orders.\n\n**2. Basket records, for each creation unit purchased or redeemed**\n- The names and quantities of the positions in the basket exchanged.\n- Whether the basket was a **custom basket**, and a record stating that it complied with the ETF's custom-basket policies and procedures under Rule 6c-11(c)(3).\n- Any cash balancing amount.\n- The identity of the AP transacting with the ETF.\n\n**Retention period**\n- The records must be kept for **at least five years**.\n- For the **first two years**, they must be in an **easily accessible place**.\n\nTo my knowledge, these requirements are unchanged since the rule was adopted in 2019. Check for any recent SEC amendments before relying on this.","ttft_ms":4007,"type":"result","duration_ms":6363,"uuid":"8e9c95c2-e2d6-4c32-aef5-cedead1b15b2","ttft_stream_ms":1097,"time_to_request_ms":61,"first_content_frame_ms":1097,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
